      "description": "This German military cemetery can be found in Ysselsteyn in the Province of Limburg close to the German border. The cemetery is the only German military cemetery in the Netherlands. 85 killed soldiers from the First World War and almost 32.000 from the Second World War are buried here. For each killed soldier one grey cross has been placed. There are approximately 5000 unknown soldiers buried on this cemetery. These are buried in graves with crosses on which it reads ’Ein Deutscher Soldat’.",
